### =============================================================================
### Runnable request collection (IntelliJ HTTP Client / VS Code "REST Client").
### Start the platform first:  docker compose --profile apps up -d --build
### =============================================================================

@gateway = http://localhost:8080
@orders  = http://localhost:8081
@auth    = http://localhost:9000

### 1. Token via CLIENT CREDENTIALS (service-to-service; sub = machine-client)
# @name token
POST {{auth}}/oauth2/token
Authorization: Basic machine-client machine-secret
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

grant_type=client_credentials&scope=orders.read orders.write

> {% client.global.set("token", response.body.access_token); %}

### 2. OpenID discovery + public signing keys
GET {{auth}}/.well-known/openid-configuration

###
GET {{auth}}/oauth2/jwks

### 3. Place an order (idempotent: re-send it with the same key and you get the same order back, 200)
# @name placeOrder
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-order-0001

{
  "shippingAddress": {"street": "1 Main St", "city": "Amsterdam", "postalCode": "1011", "country": "NL"},
  "items": [{"sku": "SKU-0001", "quantity": 2}, {"sku": "SKU-COFFEE", "quantity": 3}],
  "discountCode": "COFFEE3FOR2",
  "metadata": {"channel": "mobile", "campaign": "black-friday"}
}

> {% client.global.set("orderId", response.body.id); %}

### 4. Read it: version 1 (default) vs version 2 (adds the status history)
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

###
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
X-API-Version: 2

### 5. My orders, keyset pagination (pass nextCursor from the response as ?cursor=...)
GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/mine?size=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 6. GraphQL: select exactly the fields you need; lines are batch-loaded
POST {{gateway}}/graphql
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"query": "{ myOrders(limit: 5) { id status total { amount currency } lines { sku quantity lineTotal } history { toStatus changedAt } } }"}

### 7. Cancel (triggers the compensating StockReleased in inventory-service)
POST {{gateway}}/api/orders/{{orderId}}/cancel
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{"reason": "changed my mind"}

### 8. Validation error → RFC 9457 Problem Details (400)
POST {{orders}}/api/orders
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-invalid-0001

{"shippingAddress": {"street": "", "city": "X", "postalCode": "1", "country": "Netherlands"}, "items": [{"sku": "bad", "quantity": 0}]}

### 9. Partner webhook with an API key (custom security filter)
POST {{orders}}/api/webhooks/payments
X-API-Key: local-dev-partner-key
Content-Type: application/json

{"providerEventId": "evt_123", "orderId": "{{orderId}}", "status": "PAID"}

### 10. Public catalog through the gateway (HTTP-cacheable) + the deprecated legacy route
GET {{gateway}}/api/products/SKU-0001/price

###
GET {{gateway}}/legacy/catalog/SKU-0001

### 11. Catalog analytics (MongoDB aggregation pipeline with $lookup)
GET http://localhost:8082/api/products/analytics/categories

### 12. Actuator
GET {{orders}}/actuator/health/readiness

###
GET {{orders}}/actuator/prometheus

### 13. Admin-only endpoints need a user with ROLE_ADMIN (bob). Use the authorization-code flow with PKCE
###     (client shop-web) from a browser or Postman, then:
# GET {{gateway}}/api/orders?status=CONFIRMED&minTotal=100&page=0&size=20
# GET {{gateway}}/api/orders/reports/daily-revenue?from=2026-01-01&to=2026-12-31
